  "ai_language_tip": "Start in Georgian (ka); Russian is understood by many older people and in tourism, English increasingly by younger staff in Tbilisi and Batumi. Follow the language the other side chooses.",
  "english_ok": "sometimes — Common among younger staff in Tbilisi, Batumi and tourist venues; limited in clinics, garages and villages.",
  "politeness": "Warm and hospitable; respectful 'თქვენ'; open with 'გამარჯობა'; address as 'ბატონო …' (men) / 'ქალბატონო …' (women) + first name; close with 'მადლობა, ნახვამდის'.",
  "name_tip": "Bookings under first name with 'ბატონი'/'ქალბატონი', or surname (often ending -შვილი, -ძე, -ია, not gendered); spell Latin names slowly.",
  "phone_tip": "Mobile 5XX XX XX XX (9 digits, e.g. 5XX 12345678), Tbilisi landline 032 2XX XX XX, international +995; WhatsApp and Viber common.",
  "time_tip": "Watch out: 'რვის ნახევარი' = 7:30 (half of eight); 'შვიდის ნახევარი' = 6:30; written 24h ('19:30'); read back in 24h.",
  "number_tip": "Georgian counting is vigesimal (base 20): 'ოთხმოცდაათი' = 90 (four-twenty-and-ten); read numbers digit by digit or in small groups to avoid confusion.",
  "avoid_calling": "Avoid restaurant peaks and late evening; Sundays for offices; Orthodox Christmas (7 January) and Easter periods.",
  "closed_days": "Shops and restaurants open daily; offices closed weekends; holidays include 1–2 January, 7 and 19 January, 3 and 8 March, 9 April, Orthodox Easter (moves), 9, 12 and 26 May, 28 August, 14 October, 23 November.",
  "booking_channels": "Rezto and Myjavshani for restaurants, salons and clinics; BigMed and REDMED-type apps for doctors; Wolt, Glovo and Bolt Food for delivery; Bolt and Yandex Go for taxis; phone, WhatsApp and Facebook/Instagram messages very common.",
  "voice_menu": "Magti, Silknet, Cellfie, banks and utilities use IVR; restaurants and small clinics answer directly.",
  "callback_habits": "Small businesses confirm by call or WhatsApp/Viber; platforms send SMS.",
